# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RDRS Monitoring MIS — environment
# Copy to `.env.local` for local development. On Vercel, set these in the
# project's Settings → Environment Variables.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Postgres connection string.
#
# LEAVE THIS UNSET for a zero-setup local run: the app falls back to an
# embedded PostgreSQL 16 (PGlite) persisted to ./.pglite-data. No Docker, no
# local Postgres server, no signup.
#
# SET IT for any real deployment. Provision it from the Vercel dashboard:
#   Project → Storage → Marketplace → Neon (free tier, billed to this account)
# Vercel injects DATABASE_URL automatically once the integration is connected,
# so in that case you do not need to add it by hand.
# DATABASE_URL="postgres://user:password@host/db?sslmode=require"

# Optional: where the embedded Postgres keeps its files (default ./.pglite-data).
# PGLITE_DIR=""

# Signing key for the session cookie. REQUIRED in production — without it the
# app falls back to a development secret and logs a warning.
# Generate with:  openssl rand -base64 32
# SESSION_SECRET=""

# Set to 1 to render the current access codes on the login screen.
# Convenient for demos; do not enable on a shared deployment.
# SHOW_DEMO_CODES=""
